Shafaq News- Baghdad Iraqi Prime Minister Ali Al-Zaidi revealed on Friday that Iraq narrowly avoided international isolation, coming &ldquo;within days&rdquo; of facing sanctions and the withdrawal o
In an interview with state-run Al-Iraqiya TV, Al-Zaidi explained that Western governments had viewed Iraq as &ldquo;a state controlled by armed factions,&rdquo; but his administration had managed to avert the threat, saying that three armed groups had agreed to place their weapons under state control, while negotiations with four others remained underway. &ldquo;By June 30 , 2027, no weapons will remain outside state authority.&rdquo;
Characterizing the decision as irreversible, he said the departure of foreign troops had removed &ldquo;a longstanding justification&rdquo; for armed factions to retain their weapons. He also asserted that no US military personnel, including advisers, remained in Iraq.
